  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_0' aria-label=\" Darubai & Anr.  versus Kamalabai & Ors. pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('0','2026','2026_7_1_10','2026INSC613'); ><font size='4'> <strong>DARUBAI & ANR. <span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>KAMALABAI & ORS. </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 7 S.C.R. 1</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 613</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010001842026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : SANJAY KAROL<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, AUGUSTINE GEORGE MASIH</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Whether the defendant could avail the ground of legal necessity as &lsquo;karta&rsquo; of the family, and whether the parties to the lis, would succeed to the suit properties as tenants in common or joint tenants, since their rights flow from s.8 of the Hindu Succession &ndash; s.8 &ndash; The four plaintiffs including the present respondent had filed suit for partition and separate possession claiming to be 4/5th owners of the property of late Da, being the successors-in-interest as his daughters along with Di, who is the wife of Da &ndash; In other words,<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 01-06-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 8358/2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Dismissed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('0','2026','2026_7_1_10','2026INSC613','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outl